==Synopsis==
==Principal characters==
*'''[[Empress Elisabeth of Austria|Elisabeth]]''', the Empress of Austria and later Queen of Hungary. Nickname is Sisi. Her birthplace is the [[Kingdom of Bavaria]] in [[Germany]].
*'''[[Personifications of death|Death]]''', the personification of the abstract concept of "[[Death]]" or the "[[Grim Reaper]]". His appearance is modeled on the poet [[Heinrich Heine]] who was fascinated by Elisabeth, and the rock singer [[David Bowie]].
*'''[[Luigi Lucheni]]''', an [[Italians|Italian]] anarchist and Elisabeth's assassin. He serves as the narrator in the story, quick to point out Elisabeth's flaws and fallibility.
*[[Franz Joseph I of Austria|'''Franz Joseph''']], the Emperor of Austria and later King of Hungary. Husband of Elisabeth.
*[[Princess Sophie of Bavaria|'''Archduchess Sophie''']], Franz Joseph's domineering mother.
*[[Rudolf, Crown Prince of Austria|'''Rudolf''']], Elisabeth and Franz Joseph's son.
*[[Duke Maximilian Joseph in Bavaria|'''Max''']], Prince of the Kingdom of Bavaria in Germany. Elisabeth's neglectful father that she nonetheless idolizes.
*[[Princess Ludovika of Bavaria|'''Ludovika''']], Princess of the Kingdom of Bavaria in Germany. Elisabeth's social-climbing mother and Sophie's younger sister.
*[[Duchess Helene in Bavaria|'''Helene''']], Elisabeth's demure and ladylike elder sister.
*'''[[Irma Sztáray|Countess Esterházy]]''', the Mistress of the Household.
*[[Karl Ludwig von Grünne|'''Count Grünne''']], Franz Joseph's advisor.
*'''[[Joseph Othmar Rauscher|Cardinal Archbishop Rauscher]]''', the head of the Roman Catholic Church in Austria.
*'''[[Prince Felix of Schwarzenberg|Prince Schwarzenberg]]''', the State Minister.
*'''[[:de:Johanna_Wolf_(Bordellbetreiberin)|Frau Wolf]]''', the mistress of a brothel in Vienna.

